    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d160">

                <pb facs="0444" n="396" sameAs="frus:frus1868p1/pg396"/>

                <head>Mr. Johnson to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 96.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1869-01-09"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 9, 1869.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Until I hear from you in answer to my
                    dispatches Nos. 86 and 87, of the dates respectively of the 23d and 24th of
                    December, I can make no further progress with the claims question. If your reply
                    shall substantially comply with the suggestions of Lord Clarendon as to the mode
                    of settling the Alabama claims, I have no doubt that I shall be able to conclude
                    an arrangement which will be satisfactory to the President and yourself and the
                    Senate, at so early a day that the controversy may be finally closed during the
                    present session of Congress.</p>
                <p>Awaiting your next dispatches upon the subject, I remain, with high regard, your
                    obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>REVERDY JOHNSON.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
